{{!
    @template local_catquizlab/plansteps

    Defining an experiment, as the eight decisions it actually is.

    The editor is one long form, which is honest about the data and unhelpful
    about the work. This says which decisions have been made and which is next,
    without hiding a field or moving one.

    Classes required for JS: none.
    Data attributes required for JS: none.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * steps - number, label, done, pending
    * done, total - how far along
    * nextlabel - the first thing still to do
    * hasruns, progressurl - where to go once the runs exist

    Example context (json):
    {
        "steps": [
            {"id": "basics", "number": 1, "label": "1. Name and purpose", "done": true, "pending": false},
            {"id": "model", "number": 2, "label": "2. Model and strategy", "done": false, "pending": true}
        ],
        "done": 1,
        "total": 8,
        "ready": false,
        "hasruns": false,
        "runs": 0,
        "nextlabel": "Next: 2. Model and strategy",
        "progressurl": "/local/catquizlab/runs.php?experimentid=1"
    }
}}
<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h3 class="h6">{{#str}}plan:heading, local_catquizlab{{/str}}</h3>
        <ol class="list-unstyled mb-2 small">
            {{#steps}}
                <li class="{{#pending}}text-muted{{/pending}}">
                    {{#done}}&check;{{/done}}{{#pending}}&nbsp;&nbsp;{{/pending}} {{label}}
                </li>
            {{/steps}}
        </ol>
        <p class="small mb-1"><strong>{{nextlabel}}</strong></p>
        {{#hasruns}}
            <a href="{{progressurl}}" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary">
                {{#str}}plan:toprogress, local_catquizlab{{/str}}
            </a>
        {{/hasruns}}
    </div>
</div>
